Subject: [PATCH 4/6] geph5-app: implement `register` against the query engine

The proof-of-work puzzle is solved inside the query engine, not in the CLI, so
this starts registration remotely and polls for progress. On Android this
matters more than elsewhere: there is no browser to hand the signup page to,
so in-module registration is the only way a phone user can get an account.

Depends on the Register variant from patch 3 and on
platform::engine_control(EngineRole::Query) from patch 6; it will not compile
until patch 6 is applied too. Patch *application*, however, is independent per
file, which is the point of the split.
